        <briefdescription>
<para>Starts the monitoring thread. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Starts the monitoring thread that periodically checks a pooled connection.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::logic_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If a monitor thread appears already joinable (a fresh object has none, so this guard is effectively inactive on construction).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The loop leases a connection through a <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> (so it is returned on scope exit), checks it, and on failure reconnects it and then asks the pool to reconnect all idle connections. <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref>, a lost connection and any other exception are logged (or warned) and followed by an interval sleep, so one bad cycle cannot spin the loop. The thread reads the atomic stop flag each iteration. <parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::logic_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If a monitor thread is already joinable. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
