        <briefdescription>
<para>Signals the monitor thread to stop and joins it before returning. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Stops the monitor and waits for its thread to finish.</para>
<para>The atomic flag is cleared first so the loop exits at its next iteration; join then guarantees the thread is no longer using <computeroutput>this</computeroutput> before destruction. This must happen before the pool the thread borrows from is torn down. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
